^.*\.Rproj$
^\.Rproj\.user$
^_pkgdown\.yml$
^docs$
^pkgdown$
^\.github$
^results.*$
^README\.Rmd$
# The full-resolution logo masters (1.6 MB PNG + 4 MB SVG). They stay in the
# repository as the source of truth for the artwork, but shipping them would
# put the installed package over the 5 MB size threshold for the sake of an
# image nothing in the package reads. The 250 px man/figures/logo.png is the
# copy that ships, and is what the README and the pkgdown site use.
^inst/assets$
# The full GPL-3 text. GitHub detects the licence from a file named LICENSE, so
# it stays at that name in the repository -- but DESCRIPTION declares
# "License: GPL (>= 3)" without "+ file LICENSE", and a LICENSE file inside the
# tarball is then read as a licence stub that does not parse. Kept in the repo,
# out of the build.
^LICENSE$
^LICENSE\.md$
^\.Rhistory$
^cran-comments\.md$
^CRAN-SUBMISSION$
^codecov\.yml$
^\.lintr$
^benchmark$
^logo$
^PUBLISHING\.md$
# GitHub reads CITATION.cff from the REPOSITORY to render the "Cite this
# repository" box, never from the tarball, so shipping it gains nothing and
# R CMD check lists any unrecognised top-level file as a non-standard one.
# inst/CITATION is the copy that ships and is what citation("cyRAVEN") reads.
^CITATION\.cff$
# Docker build-context exclusions. Read by `docker build`, never by R, and
# R CMD check reports any hidden top-level file as probably included in error.
^\.dockerignore$
# The worked-example article and its 19 rendered figures. pkgdown builds articles
# from this source tree, so the published site carries them; the tarball does
# not, because self-contained HTML embeds every image and would add about 5 MB to
# the installed package for documentation nobody reads from an R session.
^vignettes/figures\.Rmd$
^vignettes/figures$
# Claude Code skill. Documentation for humans and agents, published through the
# pkgdown article rather than shipped in the tarball.
^\.claude$
# Working notes and the demonstration cohort from the README quick start. The
# latter is downloaded public FCS and is regenerated by inst/scripts/demo_data.R.
^TODO\.md$
^commit\.txt$
^demo$
